+HTTP endpoints expose health, the authenticated actor, and a tenant-scoped read-only certificate list with learner-name/serial search, sorting, and pagination. Authenticated course options and course-based bulk issuance are available. Bulk issuance snapshots course enrollments and processes each independently, using the same tenant-scoped lock and issuance transaction. It returns issued, skipped (incomplete, already issued, or revoked), and failed outcomes; concurrent/repeated requests create at most one certificate and one issuance audit event per enrollment. Revocation endpoints, exports, and administrative CRUD remain future scopes. The browser list accepts a generated admin token in memory without a login page. No automatic business-data cache is introduced. Migration rollout and seed execution are explicit actions; the running development database is not changed by implementation verification.
