README.md:3:Training admin demo with tenant-scoped data models, transactional certificate issuance/revocation services, generated bearer-token actor identification, and a repeatable demo seed. The frontend includes a certificate list with learner-name/serial search, sorting and pagination, plus course-based bulk issuance with per-learner outcomes. `GET /api/health` reports process availability, not database connectivity. See [data model and invariants](docs/data-model.md).
README.md:141:`GET /api/actor` requires `Authorization: Bearer <token>` and returns only admin ID, tenant ID and name. There is no login UI. Open the certificate list and supply a generated admin token using the inline API token control. Tokens stay in memory and are cleared on reload; they are never stored in browser storage or URLs. Bulk issuance is available through the course selector and an authenticated HTTP route; revocation remains a backend service without an HTTP route. Future protected routes must use `ActorGuard` and pass its actor to the services. Tokens have no expiry in this demo; replace an admin's token hash to rotate/revoke access. Never embed tokens in frontend source or URLs.
