README.md:184:Supply a generated admin token in the existing API token control, choose a course in **Bulk issuance**, and select **Issue to eligible learners**. The course control and submit button are disabled while processing. The page shows processing status, completion totals, and one outcome for every enrollment in the course at request start. A completed request refreshes the certificate list without changing its search or sorting.
README.md:193:This implementation processes learners sequentially in one HTTP request. There is no background worker, durable batch record, progress polling, or recovery of previous per-request outcomes after reload. Keep the page open for results. A lost response or navigation can leave the result unknown while server processing continues; retrying is safe because certificate issuance is idempotent. Large courses may outlast infrastructure request timeouts. Results are held in browser memory and cleared when changing the course or token. No schema migration or business-data cache is needed.
